const content = `<p><em>Bengaluru holds a quarter of India’s AI jobs. Most courses sold into that market still stop where the hiring actually starts.</em></p><p>There is no shortage of AI training in Bangalore. There is a shortage of AI training that reaches production.</p><p>That distinction has become the deciding factor in 2026 hiring, and it is invisible on the sales pages that most candidates read before they pay.</p><p>An analysis of nine AI programs available to Bangalore learners, scored on their published module lists rather than their landing pages, found that six teach no MLOps or LLMOps at all. Two flagship programs marketed as Generative AI courses never name retrieval-augmented generation as a taught topic.</p><p>The gap matters because of where the demand has gone.</p><h2 id="the-city-is-not-short-of-ai-jobs">The City Is Not Short of AI Jobs</h2><p>Bangalore holds <strong>25.4%</strong> of every active AI job opening in India, the highest share of any city, according to <a href="https://www.peoplematters.in/news/ai-and-emerging-tech/only-three-cities-dominate-ai-job-demand-in-india-cbre-report-48487" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer">CBRE research published in February 2026</a>. Delhi NCR follows at 24.8%, Mumbai at 19.2%.</p><p>Global capability centres drive most of it. Bengaluru accounts for <strong>30% of India’s GCC hiring</strong> in 2026, up 10% year on year, and <strong>64% of new GCC roles</strong> require AI, data science or intelligent automation skills, per <a href="https://www.businesstoday.in/jobs/story/at-5-1-lakh-jobs-indias-global-capability-centre-hiring-boom-scales-new-peak-540328-2026-07-01" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer">foundit data reported in July 2026</a>. India now hosts 2,117 GCCs, of which more than 1,200 have embedded AI capability, holding roughly 250,000 AI professionals, per the <a href="https://zinnov.com/centers-of-excellence/zinnov-nasscom-india-gcc-landscape-2026-report/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer">nasscom and Zinnov India GCC Landscape Report 2026</a>. Karnataka alone accounts for close to 30% of India’s AI-related GCC hiring.</p><p>Nationally, AI and ML job postings grew <strong>25% year on year</strong> in June 2026, against 6% for white-collar hiring overall, per <a href="https://www.naukri.com/blog/naukri-jobspeak-white-collar-hiring-grows-6-in-june-2026-ai-ml-and-fresher-hiring-lead-the-charge/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer">Naukri JobSpeak</a>.</p><p>What is scarce is the candidate who can pass the interview. Quess Corp research from June 2026 puts India’s AI workforce at 920,000, of which only 257,600 sit in core AI roles. The same study found that just <strong>5% of senior tech leaders</strong> have run AI in production at enterprise scale.</p><p>That single number is why operations skills now decide the offer.</p><h2 id="two-of-the-five-fastest-growing-roles-are-operations-roles">Two of the Five Fastest-Growing Roles Are Operations Roles</h2><p>CIEL HR analysed 450 million job postings between March 2024 and May 2026.</p><table><thead><tr><th><p>Role</p></th><th><p>Demand growth, 2024 to 2026</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p>Agentic AI engineers</p></td><td><p><strong>+260%</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>GenAI solutions architects</p></td><td><p>+120%</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>AI product owners</p></td><td><p>+120%</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>LLM engineers</p></td><td><p>+86.5%</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>MLOps engineers</p></td><td><p>+82.2%</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p><em>Source: </em><a href="https://www.businesstoday.in/jobs/story/ai-job-shift-agentic-ai-engineers-emerge-as-the-hottest-tech-hire-demand-up-260-percent-553968-2026-09-08" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer"><em>CIEL HR, reported September 2026</em></a><em>.</em></p><p>LinkedIn’s Skills on the Rise 2026 list for India names prompt engineering, workflow automation and LLMOps among the fastest-rising skills nationally. Building a model in a notebook is a 2021 skill. Shipping it, versioning it, monitoring it and controlling its running cost is what a Bengaluru GCC pays for in 2026.</p><h2 id="where-the-nine-programs-actually-stand">Where the Nine Programs Actually Stand</h2><p>Fees, durations and module lists below were taken from official pages in September 2026.</p><table><thead><tr><th><p>#</p></th><th><p>Program</p></th><th><p>Provider</p></th><th><p>Duration</p></th><th><p>Listed fee</p></th><th><p>Bangalore classroom</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>1</strong></p></td><td><p><a href="https://www.learnbay.co/genai-and-agentic-ai-master-program" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GenAI and Agentic AI Master Program</a></p></td><td><p><strong>Learnbay + IBM</strong></p></td><td><p>9 months, 300+ live hrs</p></td><td><p>INR 1,59,000 + GST</p></td><td><p>Yes, hybrid</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>2</p></td><td><p>Advanced Certification in Agentic and Generative AI</p></td><td><p>TalentSprint with IISc Blr</p></td><td><p>6 months, 105 hrs</p></td><td><p>INR 3,20,000</p></td><td><p>Yes, 4 campus days</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>3</p></td><td><p>Executive PG in Applied AI and Agentic AI</p></td><td><p>upGrad with IIIT Bangalore</p></td><td><p>2.5 years</p></td><td><p>INR 1,40,000 incl. taxes</p></td><td><p>Yes</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>4</p></td><td><p>PGP in Generative AI and Agentic AI</p></td><td><p>Edureka + Illinois Tech</p></td><td><p>6 months</p></td><td><p>INR 1,99,999 incl. GST</p></td><td><p>No</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>5</p></td><td><p>Full Stack Applied AI Course</p></td><td><p>AnalytixLabs</p></td><td><p>3.5 months</p></td><td><p>INR 71,100 to 86,440</p></td><td><p>No</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>6</p></td><td><p>PGP in AI and Machine Learning</p></td><td><p>Great Learning + UT Austin</p></td><td><p>23 weeks</p></td><td><p>USD 3,950</p></td><td><p>No, discontinued</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>7</p></td><td><p>Artificial Intelligence Engineer Course</p></td><td><p>DataMites</p></td><td><p>9 months</p></td><td><p>INR 63,835 to 95,807</p></td><td><p>Yes</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>8</p></td><td><p>Professional Certificate in AI and ML</p></td><td><p>Simplilearn + Michigan Eng</p></td><td><p>24 weeks</p></td><td><p>USD 3,690</p></td><td><p>No</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>9</p></td><td><p>Executive Certification in GenAI and ML</p></td><td><p>Intellipaat + IIT Indore</p></td><td><p>7 months</p></td><td><p>Not published</p></td><td><p>No</p></td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="the-operations-layer-program-by-program">The Operations Layer, Program by Program</h2><p>This is the table most comparisons leave out.</p><table><thead><tr><th><p>Program</p></th><th><p>MLOps</p></th><th><p>LLMOps</p></th><th><p>Platform architecture</p></th><th><p>Deployment stack taught</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p><strong>Learnbay</strong></p></td><td><p>Yes, CI/CD for AI</p></td><td><p>Yes, 1-month module</p></td><td><p>Yes, 1.5-month module</p></td><td><p>GenAI microservices, cloud, monitoring, AWS, MLFlow, FastAPI, Docker</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Edureka + Illinois Tech</p></td><td><p>Yes</p></td><td><p>Yes, full module</p></td><td><p>No</p></td><td><p>Docker, containerisation, scaling</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>upGrad + IIIT Bangalore</p></td><td><p>Yes, full module</p></td><td><p>Partial</p></td><td><p>No</p></td><td><p>AWS, Docker, SageMaker, MLflow</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>TalentSprint + IISc</p></td><td><p>No</p></td><td><p>Yes, LLMOps module</p></td><td><p>No</p></td><td><p>Quantisation, serving frameworks</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Great Learning</p></td><td><p>Partial</p></td><td><p>No</p></td><td><p>No</p></td><td><p>Docker, Streamlit, Flask</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>AnalytixLabs</p></td><td><p>No</p></td><td><p>Partial</p></td><td><p>No</p></td><td><p>FastAPI, Streamlit, Gradio, LangSmith</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>DataMites</p></td><td><p>No</p></td><td><p>No</p></td><td><p>No</p></td><td><p>Flask, AWS EC2, Azure ML Studio</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Simplilearn</p></td><td><p>No</p></td><td><p>No</p></td><td><p>No</p></td><td><p>Gradio only</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Intellipaat</p></td><td><p>No</p></td><td><p>No</p></td><td><p>No</p></td><td><p>Gradio only</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Learnbay is the only provider here that runs AI System Architecture and Platform Engineering as a separate module on top of a dedicated LLMOps and Production Deployment module. That is the layer where AIOps sits, and most syllabi skip it entirely.</p><p>Simplilearn and Intellipaat stop at Gradio, a prototyping interface rather than a deployment stack. DataMites, which otherwise offers the broadest classical coverage available offline in Bangalore, teaches no deployment or monitoring content at all.</p><h2 id="retrieval-and-governance-are-also-uneven">Retrieval and Governance Are Also Uneven</h2><p>Two further findings emerge from the same read.</p><p><strong>RAG is absent by name from two flagship GenAI programs.</strong> Neither Simplilearn’s nor Intellipaat’s main technical syllabus lists retrieval-augmented generation as a taught topic, despite both being sold as Generative AI courses. Learnbay, upGrad with IIIT Bangalore, Edureka and AnalytixLabs all teach it as a named module.</p><p><strong>Responsible AI is graded in only four of the nine.</strong> That is a live gap given the India AI Governance Guidelines released by MeitY in February 2026, which name AI governance capacity as a national priority.</p><h2 id="software-engineers-are-poorly-served-by-most-of-the-market">Software Engineers Are Poorly Served by Most of the Market</h2><p>Most AI courses are structured for analysts moving into data science. A developer with three years of Java or Python experience does not need six weeks of descriptive statistics. That developer needs to build LLM services, design retrieval microservices, orchestrate multi-agent workflows, and still clear a data structures and system design round at a product company.</p><p>Only one program in this comparison is built around that path. Learnbay’s <a href="https://www.learnbay.co/artificial-intelligence/sde-master-program-genai-agentic-ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SDE Master Program in Generative AI and Agentic AI</a> runs seven modules over 7 to 8 months and adds full modules on Data Structures and Algorithms and System Design alongside GenAI, Agentic AI and LLMOps. Six 40-hour electives sit on top, including Backend Engineering for LLM Applications and RAG Microservices, and Distributed Systems and Microservices for AI Applications.</p><p>No other provider in this set offers those as taught electives.</p><h2 id="classroom-access-is-narrower-than-the-listicles-suggest">Classroom Access Is Narrower Than the Listicles Suggest</h2><p>Only four options have a genuine Bangalore presence: Learnbay with hybrid project sessions at HSR Layout, DataMites at BTM Layout, Marathahalli and Kudlu Gate, Talentsprint with IISc for four campus days, and 360DigiTMG at Yelahanka for its Advanced Program only.</p><p>Great Learning has discontinued its Bangalore classroom, and the old programme URL now redirects to an inactive page. AnalytixLabs runs classroom batches in Gurgaon and Noida only, despite an HSR Layout address in its site footer. Edureka, Simplilearn and upGrad have no classroom anywhere.</p><h2 id="what-to-verify-before-paying">What to Verify Before Paying</h2><ol><li>Does the module list name RAG, fine-tuning and agents, or only “Generative AI”?</li><li>Is there a graded LLMOps or MLOps module, or does the course end at the notebook?</li><li>Is responsible AI taught as a module, or as a single bullet?</li><li>Is the fee published in INR on the page, or hidden behind a form?</li><li>How many hours are live, and how many are recorded?</li><li>Do projects finish as a deployed service, or as a Jupyter file?</li><li>Does the career page say “assistance” or “guarantee”, and what does the contract say?</li></ol><p>On that last point, every program in this comparison uses assistance wording. None guarantees a job. Any provider that promises one deserves a closer read of its contract.</p><p>A useful single question for any counsellor: which module teaches a learner to monitor a deployed LLM application and control its token cost? The answer reveals whether the course ends at the notebook.</p><h2 id="faqs">FAQs</h2><p><strong>Which AI course in Bangalore is best in 2026?</strong> It depends on the profile. Working professionals who want Generative AI, Agentic AI and production operations in one track with classroom access are best served by Learnbay’s GenAI and Agentic AI Master Program. Engineers who already know machine learning and want research-grade depth on agents should look at IISc Bangalore. Those on a budget under INR 1 lakh get the most agent tooling from AnalytixLabs.</p><p><strong>Do AI courses in Bangalore teach MLOps and LLMOps?</strong> Most do not. Six of the nine programs compared teach no production operations at all, and only three run a named LLMOps module like Learnbay and upGrad. Given that MLOps engineer demand grew 82.2% between 2024 and 2026, this is the most expensive gap a syllabus can carry.</p><p><strong>What salary follows an AI course in Bangalore?</strong> Entry-level AI roles in India pay INR 8.87 to 15.41 LPA, and senior roles in Bengaluru reach INR 61.70 to 91.25 LPA, per foundit data from September 2026. <a href="https://www.business-standard.com/finance/personal-finance/36-lakh-vs-26-lakh-ai-skills-now-command-a-38-salary-premium-over-it-126071600178_1.html" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer">1 Finance Research</a> puts the AI premium over traditional IT at 33% at 3 to 5 years of experience and 38% beyond 10 years.</p><p><em>Fees, durations and syllabus details were taken from official program pages in September 2026 and are subject to change. No provider in this comparison guarantees employment.</em></p>`;

export default content;
